The updateContent and mouseout handlers in the wiki webview entry point must call clearHoverState() from the tooltip module to cancel the hover timer, clear the pending-hover anchor reference, and hide the tooltip — preventing stale hover state from referencing a morphdom-detached anchor element after content patching. Nothing checks that either handler calls it, so removing a call silently re-introduces the stale-hover-tooltip bug.
